From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 19:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: dma: apple,sio: Add the S5L8960X

The A7's SmartIO (Apple's iop,s5l8960x) is an AppleA7IOP with the
version 1 register layout of the T7000: one 0x2000 window, four
interrupts, and no shim registers in Apple's device tree. Add
apple,s5l8960x-sio to the single-window variants.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/dma/apple,sio.yaml | 12 +++++++-----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/dma/apple,sio.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/dma/apple,sio.yaml
index b19e66a2a..586739b18 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/dma/apple,sio.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/dma/apple,sio.yaml
@@ -4,11 +4,11 @@
 $id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/dma/apple,sio.yaml#
 $schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
 
-title: Apple T7000/S8000/T8010 SmartIO coprocessor and DMA controller
+title: Apple S5L8960X/T7000/S8000/T8010 SmartIO coprocessor and DMA controller
 
 description: |
-  The T7000 (A8, A8X), S8000 (A9) and T8010 (A10) SmartIO coprocessor
-  provides DMA channels
+  The S5L8960X (A7), T7000 (A8, A8X), S8000 (A9) and T8010 (A10) SmartIO
+  coprocessor provides DMA channels
   for peripheral controllers. The application processor boots the SmartIO
   firmware and submits DMA commands through the SIO message queues. Clients
   select the firmware endpoint number used by their peripheral.
@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@ allOf:
 properties:
   compatible:
     enum:
+      - apple,s5l8960x-sio
       - apple,t7000-sio
       - apple,s8000-sio
       - apple,t8010-sio
@@ -80,8 +81,9 @@ then:
       minItems: 2
 else:
   description:
-    The T7000's AppleA7IOP version 1 block is a single 0x2000 window, and
-    Apple's device tree describes no shim registers for it.
+    The S5L8960X's and T7000's AppleA7IOP version 1 block is a single
+    0x2000 window, and Apple's device tree describes no shim registers for
+    it.
   properties:
     reg:
       maxItems: 1
-- 
